  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Juggle it over to your partner",
  "description": "Pairs with one ball, 3–5 metres apart. With an odd number of players, make one group of three. Keep the ball in the air and play it between you – with your feet, thighs and head.\n\nRun it as a ladder with three steps. Step 1: the ball may bounce once between touches, and you juggle as many times as you like before you lift it over to your partner. Step 2: you have exactly two touches – one to bring the ball down and one to play it on. Step 3: one touch only, you play the ball straight back and forth. When the pair manages ten in a row, move up a step.\n\nFinish with a competition: which pair can keep it going longest on their step before the ball hits the ground? Copycat: one pair shows their own way of playing the ball between them, and the other pairs try to copy it. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Soft touches – meet the ball and lift it to about hip height."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Watch the ball as it comes, and look at your partner before you play it."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Use both feet. The thigh is good for bringing down a high ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Play the ball so it is easy for your partner to take."
    }
  ],
